silm:instances_papers_19_mereology_as_colimit_chapters_08_cheese_and_failure_modes_sections_01_cheese_trap_face_closure_concrete_anchor#mereologydiagram silm:hasLongDescription "The MereologyDiagram is the part-whole diagram of Mittens-the-cat, indexed by body-region tags (head, torso, paws, tail) and overlap joints. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'D_Mittens', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
