silm:instances_papers_19_mereology_as_colimit_chapters_08_cheese_and_failure_modes_sections_01_cheese_trap_face_closure_concrete_anchor#headobservation silm:hasLongDescription "The HeadObservation is the head-region olog fragment of Mittens's vet exam: left ear position, right ear position, three-color torbie eye markings. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'HeadObs', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
